# 🐞 bug report

### Affected Package

@angular/core, maybe @angular/compiler...

### Is this a regression?

Worked in 8 and below

### Description

A module throws when trying to create a new component instance in the constructor.

```ts
@NgModule({
  declarations: [
    FeatComponent,
  ],
  imports: [
    CommonModule
  ],
})
export class FeatModule {

  constructor(ngRef: NgModuleRef<FeatModule>) {
    // A self declared component, WONT WORK:
    try {
      ngRef.componentFactoryResolver.resolveComponentFactory(FeatComponent).create(ngRef.injector);
    } catch (err) {
      console.error(err);
    }

    // A parent declared component, WONT WORK:
     try {
      ngRef.componentFactoryResolver.resolveComponentFactory(AppComponent).create(ngRef.injector);
    } catch (err) {
      console.error(err);
    }
  }
}
```

Note that both a self declared component and a parent component will fail.

The fix in #35580 solve a portion of the issue but not all of it. (Iv'e tried to [explain it here](https://github.com/angular/angular/pull/35637#issuecomment-590115523) with no luck)

The problem starts [here](https://github.com/angular/angular/blob/master/packages/core/src/render3/ng_module_ref.ts#L55) with the root module of the app is created along with an `NgModuleRef` for it:

```ts
    this._r3Injector = createInjector(
        ngModuleType, _parent,
        [
          {provide: viewEngine_NgModuleRef, useValue: this},
          {provide: viewEngine_ComponentFactoryResolver, useValue: this.componentFactoryResolver}
        ],
        stringify(ngModuleType)) as R3Injector;
```

`ngModuleType` is the app's root module class and in this call it will go and instantiate all child modules...  (`FeatModule`).

The child module will try to create a component instance (`FeatModule.constructor`) which will
at some point require the `_r3Injector`. However, it is still not there because the original function call (`createInjector`) did not still finish (the one called from the app module root).

This definitely worked in v8.

## 🔬 Minimal Reproduction

Go to https://stackblitz.com/edit/angular-9-abstract-mv8oep?file=src%2Fapp%2Ffeat-module%2Ffeat-module.ts 

While the repro demo is using angular 9.0.0 i've verified this locally on the latest build using:

```
    "@angular/compiler": "https://github.com/angular/compiler-builds/archive/9.1.0-next.1+835618c678.tar.gz",
    "@angular/core": "https://github.com/angular/core-builds/archive/9.1.0-next.1+835618c678.tar.gz",
```

Including an ngcc rebuild.

